        ]
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "reviewer-applied-fix",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-15T10:04:00Z",
          "note": "workspaces.ts line 23: Updated JSDoc description on `registerWorkspaceRoutes()` — the old text said 'All handlers delegate to the supplied WorkspaceManager' which became inaccurate after WP-002 added launch handlers that also delegate to ProjectManager and ErrorLogManager. New text: 'Handlers delegate to the supplied WorkspaceManager, ProjectManager, and (on launch failure) ErrorLogManager'. Non-behavioral — no runtime change."
        },
        {
          "type": "documentation-forward",
          "priority": "medium",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-15T10:04:00Z",
          "note": "[documentation-forward] workspaces.ts: The optional 7th `launchFn` parameter on `registerWorkspaceRoutes()` has only a brief inline comment ('for testing only'). Add a JSDoc `@param` entry explicitly marking it as test-only, documenting its signature `(command: string, args: string[]) => Promise<void>`, and noting it defaults to `launchApplication`. This prevents future callers from using it in production code."
        },
        {
          "type": "documentation-forward",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-15T10:04:00Z",
          "note": "[documentation-forward] workspaces.ts (github-desktop handler): The `project.Repositories.includes(repoId)` check that implicitly blocks path traversal via `repoId` has no comment explaining why this is sufficient. Add a brief inline comment (e.g. '// repoId is already validated against the project allow-list, preventing path traversal') to aid future maintainers — this was flagged by both QA and Security Auditor."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-15T10:04:00Z",
          "note": "workspaces-launch.test.ts lines 32–36: The `process.on('exit', ...)` cleanup handler is redundant given the `after()` hook on lines 38–43 that also clears allTempDirs. Both are present in workspaces-health.test.ts as well (pre-existing pattern), so this is consistent, but the process.on('exit') guard is only needed if the after() hook fails. Harmless belt-and-suspenders pattern — no action required."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-15T10:04:00Z",
          "note": "workspaces.ts: The `launchFn` 7th positional parameter is pragmatic for now but will grow awkward if more injectable dependencies are added to this function. Worth noting as a future refactor target: a named options object (e.g. `{ launchFn? }`) or a proper DI approach would scale better. Not a blocker for this WP."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "status_changed_at": "2026-04-15T09:48:38Z",
  "last_updated": "2026-04-15T10:04:00Z",
  "handoff_notes": [
    {
      "from_agent": "Developer",
      "to_agent": "QA",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-15T09:58:01Z",
      "notes": [
        "\"All 8 acceptance criteria are met and verified by 14 dedicated tests in workspaces-launch.test.ts. The injectable `launchFn` parameter (7th arg, optional, defaults to real `launchApplication`) is the test seam — QA tests should use this same mechanism. The route for github-desktop does a double 404 check: first via WorkspaceManager (throws NotFoundError for unknown project), then via ProjectManager.getById (null for unknown project) + Repositories.includes (for unknown repo). The workspace file path for vscode uses the same `getWorkspaceFilePath()` helper used by the regenerate-workspace-file route.\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "from_agent": "QA",
      "to_agent": "Security Auditor",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-15T10:00:29Z",
      "notes": [
        "All 8 acceptance criteria verified and met. 733/733 tests pass. Build is clean. Two new POST routes (launch/vscode, launch/github-desktop/:rid) are correctly implemented with proper 404/400/200/500 handling and ErrorLogManager integration. No security concerns beyond what is noted in comments (existsSync-on-directory is benign; repoId traversal is blocked by existing validation). Ready for Security Audit."
      ]
    },
    {
      "from_agent": "Security Auditor",
      "to_agent": "Reviewer",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-15T10:02:23Z",
      "notes": [
        "Security audit PASS. No Critical or High findings. Two Medium observations raised (defence-in-depth path traversal hardening; error message disclosure in 500 paths) — neither blocks approval in the current localhost-only deployment context. All 8 acceptance criteria confirmed met. Ready for Code Review."
      ]
    },
    {
      "from_agent": "Reviewer",
      "to_agent": "Documentation",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-15T10:04:00Z",
      "notes": [
        "Code review PASS. All 8 AC confirmed met. One Fix-Forward applied: JSDoc description on registerWorkspaceRoutes() updated to accurately name all three delegated managers (non-behavioral). Two documentation-forward items for the Documentation agent: (1) add @param JSDoc for the test-only launchFn 7th parameter; (2) add inline comment in the github-desktop handler explaining why project.Repositories.includes(repoId) is sufficient for path traversal prevention. No blocking issues. Ready for Documentation."
      ]
    }
  ]
}

